Well, unless the patch requiring those new levels
also patched the makefile, you're maybe going to need to
add the names of the new levels to the makefile as
targets to be created. They may, however, be picked
up automatically as part of some parameterized list
of level description input files. Not having seen
the makefile for SlashEm, I've less than no clue
how/where/whether to do that. Also if, as indicated
by others elsewhere, those new levels being built
are required precursors to building the executable,
your makefile needs to have a dependency in it that
expresses that requirement, so that the makefile
will build the new levels before it attempts to use
them. If the makefile is well constructed, this
should happen by default, but it may not be that
pretty, so check it yourself to assure that such is
the case.

